Sometime last night, the high score list filled up on the sporkhack.com
server -- meaning we now have 2,000 games recorded that were at least a
single point (there are about 3,000 games in the logfile, for comparison.)
That's a lot for just four months of a new toy, really.

Overall, I mostly just wanted to thank everyone for being willing to try
this stuff out.  Not all of my changes have been (or will be) popular, and
of course a beta server occasionally has some bugs or crashes that need
to be worked out... but it seems everyone was willing to put up with the
twitchiness inbetween, and that makes me happy.

The resistance changes went in yesterday, of course.  I did try to work
around the confusion with loading a different resistance scheme from
save (as opposed to just breaking save and not having the problem), but
it looks like that didn't work out -- so if you have a save from
pre-10/29, any _eaten_ resistances are likely to show as 0%, not 100%.
Games started post-10/29 will not have this problem, so it will
work itself out rather rapidly; just be aware, is all.

There will be more coming...

